H-P2 choice points — does entropy localize the real choices, and how sparse are they?

[branch grammar K=4 seg_len=8, toy model, 400 steps]
  train loss 0.198 nats/token vs grammar floor 0.173 (ln K = 1.386 once per segment)
  entropy at true choice points 1.375 vs elsewhere 0.002 (step path)
  AUROC(entropy -> choice point): forward 1.000 | step 1.000
  fraction flagged above ln(K)/2: 0.125 (true choice fraction 0.125)

[checkpoint mh_multihorizon.pt on 4095 real positions]
  entropy median 5.61 nats, p90 7.47
  fraction above 1 / 2 / 3 nats: 0.962 / 0.919 / 0.845
  -> that fraction is the share of steps a prospection budget would open branches at

PASS: entropy is a usable choice-point detector on the toy; the budget rule has a signal.
